  "categories": {
    "rRNA": {
      "description": "Every rRNA-derived gene GENCODE v50lift37 annotates on hg19: the nuclear 5S loci, the rRNA-derived pseudogene copies, and the two mitochondrial genes MT-RNR1 (12S) and MT-RNR2 (16S). The list is deliberately inclusive, being meant for counting rRNA-derived reads as a QC metric rather than for describing rRNA biology, so a pseudogene copy that captures reads counts the same as a functional gene.",
      "source": "The gene_type attribute of the registered GTF, taking rRNA, rRNA_pseudogene and Mt_rRNA together. Two caveats matter for the metric. GENCODE annotates no 18S, 28S or 45S gene anywhere in human, so this counts 5S and 5.8S loci only; and GRCh37 carries no rDNA-bearing acrocentric sequence, so the 5.8S loci the GRCh38 annotation has are absent here. This file also annotates nine intervals twice under two gene ids, both of which are kept, so per-gene counts over those intervals overlap.",
